    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nI know this could be achieved with plugins, but maybe some built in could be interesting.\r\nRight now, when there are too much clues to show, the float can be navigated with \r\n\r\n```lua\r\nscroll_down = '<C-d>',\r\nscroll_up = '<C-u>',\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat I'm missing is some indicator that shows that _there are more keymaps that the ones shown._",
