    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI've received this feature request during beta-testing. The [reason to not add it](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/430#issuecomment-1703159812) was (and still is) that I can not come up with approach that is both concise to implement and useful. With horizontal scroll indicator there is a `extend` in 'listchars' option, which serves the purpose well, but there is nothing (as far as I know) to deal with vertical scroll.\r\n\r\nAs stated in the comment, currently suggested approach is to use default automatic height and assume that there more lines if clue window takes maximum height (from tabline to statusline). If it is shorter than that, then there are no more clues.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"good to have, but can't see good solution\". If there is some new built-in window option or anyone comes up with some appropriate approach, this can be revisited.",
